<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vira Alakeshvara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1400–1411</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vira Alakeshvara was the leading figure of the powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alagakkonara-family">Alagakkonara family</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> in the Gampola period. In 1411 the Chinese admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-he">Zheng He</a> fought his forces, captured him and took him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor">Yongle Emperor</a> later released him. His fall opened the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parakramabahu-vi">Parakramabahu VI</a> to take power at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-jayawardenepura-kotte">Kotte</a>.</p></div>
